<title>CHINA: East China wheat crop hit by drought -- paper.</title>
<headline>East China wheat crop hit by drought -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prolonged drought has hit much of the wheat crop in China's big grain-producing province of Shandong, the Dazhong Daily said.</p>
<p>The newspaper, published in the provincial capital of Jinan, said in an edition seen in Beijing on Sunday that drought had affected 1.6 million hectares, or 40 percent of the area planted with wheat in the eastern province.</p>
<p>It gave no indication of the extent of damage. No other details were given.</p>
<p>Winter wheat is the smaller of the province's two wheat crops. Shandong is also a big producer of corn.</p>
</text>
